export anchor CarbonFibreStyle:
    number: 298
    screen: CodeRepository
    name: Carbon fibre
    idea: A pit wall timing screen on woven carbon, with heavy italic condensed type, skewed tabs, a timing tower of checks, sector bars for files and motorsport red for the one thing holding the merge.
    base: dark
    palette:
        carbon: #111213, the ground under a 20px woven texture
        weaveLight: #232326, highlight threads in the weave
        panel: #1a1b1e, panels
        panelHead: #232429, panel headers and pit wall cards
        white: #f4f4f5, text, the secondary button and the focus outline
        grey: #a7a9b0, labels, meta and the outline number
        seam: #34363c, panel tops and dividers
        raceRed: #c8160c, the primary button, current tab, failing position and logo
        redLine: #ff4a3d, the header stripe, red panel tops and the focus ring
        pinkRed: #ff8278, failing and removed text on dark red
        greenFlag: #4fdc84, passed checks, the open state, approved and added lines
        amber: #ffc23d, changes requested, the team radio comment and needs QA
    type:
        A condensed sans, Helvetica Neue, Roboto Condensed, Arial Narrow, set
        italic at 800 to 900 in caps for the title at 40px, the repository
        at 26px, panel titles at 14px and buttons. The pull request number
        is a 88px italic outline figure. Body is system-ui at 14px and 1.45.
        Data and the diff use Consolas or a system monospace at 12.5 to
        13px with tabular figures.
    layout:
        The header is woven carbon with a red and white diagonal stripe at
        the right and a 3px red rule below. It holds a skewed red B logo,
        the repository in heavy italic, a Private pill and skewed counters,
        then a row of skewed tabs with the current one red. The body, also
        on carbon, has three columns. The left 240px timing tower lists
        all twelve checks with position numbers in black tabs and PASS or
        FAIL, the seventh row tinted red with a red edge and red position.
        The centre holds the lead panel with the Open flag, the title and
        the outline 214 floated right, a black gauge showing 11/12 and
        twelve skewed segments with the failing one hatched red, and two
        pit wall cards for the reviewers with green and amber left edges.
        Below are Sectors, the three files as S1 to S3 with added and
        removed bars, and Telemetry with the diff, where the comment is a
        Team radio box with an amber edge. The right 280px Race control
        panel lists assignee, skewed labels, milestone and linked issue and
        a striped disabled merge button. Below 1100px race control moves
        under, below 760px all stack.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 16px gaps between panels, 14px panel padding, tight 6px timing rows.
    density: High. Three columns with the full timing tower visible.
    corners: None. Tabs, buttons, counters, labels and segments are skewed 12 to 14 degrees instead.
    borders: A 3px seam on panel tops, red on hot panels, 4px coloured edges on pit cards and the failing row.
    shadows: None. Depth comes from the carbon weave between panels.
    icons:
        Bold 2.4px line icons. A tick with PASS, an octagon cross with FAIL,
        a ringed tick for approved, a triangle for changes requested.
    focus: A 3px white outline with a 6px red ring outside it.
    tone: Race words, such as Timing, Sectors, Telemetry, Pit wall, Team radio and Race control.
